{"Denial cache key includes ParentFolder but doesn't match cached permissions logic - denial cache stores denials at granular level (name + folder) but permission cache stores permissions at coarse level (action only), creating asymmetry where cached permissions could grant access without specifying which specific resources": 0.2412882000207901, "List operation ignores cached denials - Check consults the denial cache before authorizing, but List only uses cached or fetched permissions, so a resource denied and cached by Check can still appear in List results, creating inconsistent authorization results": 0.4856170415878296, "Denial cache key is highly granular (namespace+user+action+name+parent) but entries are never cleared - if a user is denied access to many resources, many denial cache entries are created consuming memory and preventing permission updates": 0.41127365827560425, "No mechanism exists to invalidate denial cache entries when permissions change - cannot invalidate all denial entries for a user when permissions change, or for a resource when it's shared/granted": 0.5951617360115051, "Cannot distinguish between 'user never had permission' vs 'user was just denied after previously being allowed' in the denial cache": 0.18181008100509644}